{"version":"2.1.0","runs":[{"invocations":[{"executionSuccessful":true,"toolExecutionNotifications":[]}],"results":[{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"57676cd7f763c88bcfccb9183435969f425e0850e1045da306bfb1e152f77e534ef3416e734b5373720b6778995690a8930b6cb660c1ae920a7925799903a4af_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"main.ts","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":52,"endLine":9,"snippet":{"text":"  const tmpl = Deno.readTextFileSync(\"./page.html\");"},"startColumn":16,"startLine":9}}}],"message":{"text":"A synchronous file or process call runs inside a request handler. Deno.serve handles every request on one thread, so for the duration of this call no other request makes progress — one slow disk or large file stalls the whole server. Use the async form (await Deno.readTextFile, await new Deno.Command(...).output())."},"properties":{},"ruleId":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-sync-io-in-handler"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"ce17cedf3d5bed0f7006cd0b68561ecee26abb6c28c113a3c8237bebd7d3761ddf144a3f495e2bb02631197e7b94a19ff1378769ab1c347fc9c3c43dcfcf8ce8_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"main.ts","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":45,"endLine":14,"snippet":{"text":"  const all = kv.list({ prefix: [\"users\"] });"},"startColumn":15,"startLine":14}}}],"message":{"text":"kv.list() is called inside a request handler without a `limit`. The iterator pages through every key under the selector, so one request can read the whole prefix — latency that grows with the data, and an easy way to exhaust the KV read quota. Pass {limit} and paginate with the returned cursor."},"properties":{},"ruleId":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-kv-unbounded-list"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"e64c0306298b77b94351783bcbe35d6c701341ec4349bb7a6391fab4eadf00d5935f203bd5033217903857e4f64b7da7f4aa4753c27647a4148b9912fe4e1093_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"main.ts","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":55,"endLine":19,"snippet":{"text":"  const up = await fetch(\"https://api.example.com/v1\");"},"startColumn":20,"startLine":19}}}],"message":{"text":"A request handler awaits an outbound fetch() with no AbortSignal. fetch has no default timeout, so a slow or hung upstream holds this request — and its memory and socket — open indefinitely, and enough of them exhaust the server. Pass `signal: AbortSignal.timeout(ms)`."},"properties":{},"ruleId":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-fetch-without-timeout-in-handler"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"097631848a1512fbf3c97a3ef88155ee26d1ad4905d7817dfd27eabfd8465f1d9fd49a70ea2bd73f08eec81359db971a26aa4542604a39b020b3004f678a6814_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"main.ts","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":17,"endLine":25,"snippet":{"text":"    Deno.exit(1);"},"startColumn":5,"startLine":25}}}],"message":{"text":"Deno.exit() is called inside a request handler. It terminates the whole process, so one request — possibly one an attacker can trigger at will — ends the service for every other client. Return an error Response and let the request fail on its own."},"properties":{},"ruleId":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-exit-in-handler"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"3314c20079efd33995f65abf52cbe1fa343fb8cd2e3874a0b82343789b30ed74ed2dc49db7377ffb4bbe51b672d1a91653ad1b3535d089eebe509f04ffb2efc3_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"main.ts","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":21,"endLine":36,"snippet":{"text":"  const before = hits;\n  await kv.get([\"x\"]);\n  hits = before + 1;"},"startColumn":3,"startLine":34}}}],"message":{"text":"A module-level variable is read, an await yields, and the variable is then written from the value read before the await. Deno.serve runs handlers concurrently, so another request can change the variable during the await and this write discards its update — a lost update in process memory. Do the read and the write with no await between them, or serialise the section."},"properties":{},"ruleId":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-shared-state-across-await"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"67922b887994ce4f4257a84901336e48f5562e8dae8a511be539f288f214eb051d884db82768d94c2bb766699b6d69aa8ffd06ce18fff4dd6581666f101f4b27_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"main.ts","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":40,"endLine":50,"snippet":{"text":"    out.push(await kv.get([\"user\", id]));"},"startColumn":14,"startLine":50}}}],"message":{"text":"kv.get() is awaited once per loop iteration. Each await is a round trip to the KV store (a network hop on Deno Deploy), so the loop's latency is the sum of all of them. Batch the keys with kv.getMany() (up to 10 keys per call)."},"properties":{},"ruleId":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-kv-get-in-loop"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"bd0761f51b6b0b774b432bfec69f7a3dd6f7981f1085c7b98806eec12880dcd3d767c24398aeca7d7c20d1c449c21db2cbb475773fd42a93ca98384be6980095_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"main.ts","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":43,"endLine":59,"snippet":{"text":"  Deno.writeTextFile(\"./state.json\", data);"},"startColumn":3,"startLine":59}}}],"message":{"text":"An asynchronous Deno file or KV write is started and its promise is dropped. Nothing orders it against what follows — a later read can see the old state, a later write can land first — and if it rejects, the rejection is unhandled, which terminates a Deno process. Await it, or attach a .catch() that handles the failure."},"properties":{},"ruleId":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-unawaited-write"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"0067207105af98554713967073e031ec5ffc041f853e275f44b9bcd38d1362570e58c87f9e2bf30fcce48e10b1a1bf06d9c6551aefce6265861dbfd1c98d1ae4_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"main.ts","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":26,"endLine":63,"snippet":{"text":"  kv.set([\"state\"], data);"},"startColumn":3,"startLine":63}}}],"message":{"text":"An asynchronous Deno file or KV write is started and its promise is dropped. Nothing orders it against what follows — a later read can see the old state, a later write can land first — and if it rejects, the rejection is unhandled, which terminates a Deno process. Await it, or attach a .catch() that handles the failure."},"properties":{},"ruleId":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-unawaited-write"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"c2ccbef4555bd3f712ce8a822b6d14bcb8ba59fd5ad42e339f597e3f4c828f6e6e0ccf1f65a8ec825c4aeb7a9033e89fe2c19569566d8da3ac9d0f884a4904e8_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"main.ts","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":32,"endLine":71,"snippet":{"text":"  const st = await child.status;"},"startColumn":14,"startLine":71}}}],"message":{"text":"A child process is spawned with stdout or stderr \"piped\" and that stream is never read. Once the child writes more than the pipe buffer holds (about 64 KiB on Linux) it blocks, so `await child.status` never resolves — a deadlock that small test outputs never show. Read the stream (or use child.output()), or spawn with \"null\" / \"inherit\" for output you do not need."},"properties":{},"ruleId":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-piped-output-not-read"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"e583db6335e2b5bf697842b06f477fe0559eee8797e701e7d24f3253a48716bd9da691f45c3cc120064d5947a6b1fc0788e168adb81dc4e0fb8b934c76e2139b_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"main.ts","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":120,"endLine":82,"snippet":{"text":"  const raw = new TextDecoder().decode((await new Deno.Command(\"git\", { args: [\"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"] }).output()).stdout);"},"startColumn":40,"startLine":82}}}],"message":{"text":"The output of a Deno.Command is used without checking whether the program succeeded. A failed command still resolves output() with whatever it printed, so the code proceeds on empty or partial data as if the step had worked. Check `success` (or `code`) and handle the failure using stderr."},"properties":{},"ruleId":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-command-status-unchecked"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"1921f54786927ca361de3e319cf7b72b772f16eb0eb8d352f5e1c739d5006a8085f1b52c3539e109b7fc0f183cead1996618ea7628c59f5d810b17878d62f08e_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"main.ts","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":42,"endLine":91,"snippet":{"text":"  await fetch(\"https://example.com/ping\");"},"startColumn":3,"startLine":91}}}],"message":{"text":"A fetch() response is awaited and dropped without reading or cancelling its body. The body holds the connection open until it is consumed or garbage-collected; under load the server runs out of sockets, and Deno's test sanitizer reports the leak. Read the body, or call `await res.body?.cancel()`."},"properties":{},"ruleId":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-response-body-leaked"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"c6da3c3bc28bedd8be43ee2cd09a427eda82ce1a05d62eeffe1864acb8b6bc985e57433efdd6bd16fe39bcdedc37a5651bd57f13412345fac9d7ee652ad1fddb_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"main.ts","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":34,"endLine":99,"snippet":{"text":"  const f = await Deno.open(path);"},"startColumn":3,"startLine":99}}}],"message":{"text":"A file opened with Deno.open is never closed in this function, is not declared with `using`, and its stream is not handed on (reading `file.readable` or `file.writable` to the end closes it). Each call leaks a file descriptor until the process hits its limit. Declare it with `using file = await Deno.open(...)`, or close it in a finally block."},"properties":{},"ruleId":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-file-not-closed"}],"tool":{"driver":{"name":"Opengrep OSS","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The output of a Deno.Command is used without checking whether the program succeeded. A failed command still resolves output() with whatever it printed, so the code proceeds on empty or partial data as if the step had worked. Check `success` (or `code`) and handle the failure using stderr."},"help":{"markdown":"The output of a Deno.Command is used without checking whether the program succeeded. A failed command still resolves output() with whatever it printed, so the code proceeds on empty or partial data as if the step had worked. Check `success` (or `code`) and handle the failure using stderr.","text":"The output of a Deno.Command is used without checking whether the program succeeded. A failed command still resolves output() with whatever it printed, so the code proceeds on empty or partial data as if the step had worked. Check `success` (or `code`) and handle the failure using stderr."},"id":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-command-status-unchecked","name":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-command-status-unchecked","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-252: Unchecked Return Value","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-command-status-unchecked"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"Deno.exit() is called inside a request handler. It terminates the whole process, so one request — possibly one an attacker can trigger at will — ends the service for every other client. Return an error Response and let the request fail on its own."},"help":{"markdown":"Deno.exit() is called inside a request handler. It terminates the whole process, so one request — possibly one an attacker can trigger at will — ends the service for every other client. Return an error Response and let the request fail on its own.","text":"Deno.exit() is called inside a request handler. It terminates the whole process, so one request — possibly one an attacker can trigger at will — ends the service for every other client. Return an error Response and let the request fail on its own."},"id":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-exit-in-handler","name":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-exit-in-handler","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-382: J2EE Bad Practices: Use of System.exit()","CWE-730: OWASP Top Ten 2004 Category A9 - Denial of Service","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-exit-in-handler"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"note"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A request handler awaits an outbound fetch() with no AbortSignal. fetch has no default timeout, so a slow or hung upstream holds this request — and its memory and socket — open indefinitely, and enough of them exhaust the server. Pass `signal: AbortSignal.timeout(ms)`."},"help":{"markdown":"A request handler awaits an outbound fetch() with no AbortSignal. fetch has no default timeout, so a slow or hung upstream holds this request — and its memory and socket — open indefinitely, and enough of them exhaust the server. Pass `signal: AbortSignal.timeout(ms)`.","text":"A request handler awaits an outbound fetch() with no AbortSignal. fetch has no default timeout, so a slow or hung upstream holds this request — and its memory and socket — open indefinitely, and enough of them exhaust the server. Pass `signal: AbortSignal.timeout(ms)`."},"id":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-fetch-without-timeout-in-handler","name":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-fetch-without-timeout-in-handler","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-400: Uncontrolled Resource Consumption","MEDIUM CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-fetch-without-timeout-in-handler"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A file opened with Deno.open is never closed in this function, is not declared with `using`, and its stream is not handed on (reading `file.readable` or `file.writable` to the end closes it). Each call leaks a file descriptor until the process hits its limit. Declare it with `using file = await Deno.open(...)`, or close it in a finally block."},"help":{"markdown":"A file opened with Deno.open is never closed in this function, is not declared with `using`, and its stream is not handed on (reading `file.readable` or `file.writable` to the end closes it). Each call leaks a file descriptor until the process hits its limit. Declare it with `using file = await Deno.open(...)`, or close it in a finally block.","text":"A file opened with Deno.open is never closed in this function, is not declared with `using`, and its stream is not handed on (reading `file.readable` or `file.writable` to the end closes it). Each call leaks a file descriptor until the process hits its limit. Declare it with `using file = await Deno.open(...)`, or close it in a finally block."},"id":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-file-not-closed","name":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-file-not-closed","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-775: Missing Release of File Descriptor or Handle after Effective Lifetime","MED