t()), or spawn with \"null\" / \"inherit\" for output you do not need."},"id":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-piped-output-not-read","name":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-piped-output-not-read","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-833: Deadlock","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-piped-output-not-read"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"A fetch() response is awaited and dropped without reading or cancelling its body. The body holds the connection open until it is consumed or garbage-collected; under load the server runs out of sockets, and Deno's test sanitizer reports the leak. Read the body, or call `await res.body?.cancel()`."},"help":{"markdown":"A fetch() response is awaited and dropped without reading or cancelling its body. The body holds the connection open until it is consumed or garbage-collected; under load the server runs out of sockets, and Deno's test sanitizer reports the leak. Read the body, or call `await res.body?.cancel()`.","text":"A fetch() response is awaited and dropped without reading or cancelling its body. The body holds the connection open until it is consumed or garbage-collected; under load the server runs out of sockets, and Deno's test sanitizer reports the leak. Read the body, or call `await res.body?.cancel()`."},"id":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-response-body-leaked","name":"home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-response-body-leaked","properties":{"precision":"very-high","tags":["CWE-772: Missing Release of Resource after Effective Lifetime","HIGH CONFIDENCE","security"]},"shortDescription":{"text":"Opengrep Finding: home.claude.commitwork.manifests.semgrep-deno-reliability.cw-deno-response-body-leaked"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"wa